/-- $h_{P,2}(x)=-\partial_xG_P(x)$ ([DIRX], §4, Case III), where $G_P$ is given on
$[\frac14,\frac12]$ by the formula $\frac12(Q(x)+\mathrm{J}(1-x))-2x(1-x)$ (we differentiate this
